        "# STATS 201 Week 3 · 01 Measurement\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question.** Why can the same stored answer index refer to two different labels?\n",
        "\n",
        "**How to work.** In Colab, choose **File → Save a copy in Drive**. Run the cells in order on CPU. Read the saved default outputs if Hugging Face is temporarily unavailable. Start with FOCUS = \"both\". Then display either row on its own.\n",
        "\n",
        "For Ed, share one figure or panel, a view-access link to your Colab copy, your interpretation and one check. The result displays inline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "measurement",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "measurement"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1 · Define the observed label\n",
        "\n",
        "Each record pairs a robot image with a question, choices and a stored answer. The question asks whether the black object has been moved from the bowl into the box. Read the choices and consider what evidence in the frame would support a claim of completion. The Prediction lab trains on the explicit **Yes** and **No** reference categories."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "algorithm-intuition",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "algorithm-intuition"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Measurement pseudocode and intuition\n",
        "\n",
        "The question and the options define the measurement. Here the question asks whether the robot completed the task in the selected frame. Each image–question pair stores the chosen answer as a position in its own option list. Decoding is like reading a survey answer against the exact form the respondent saw.\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "Load the two target image–question records by ID\n",
        "Select the records to display using FOCUS\n",
        "FOR each displayed record i\n",
        "    Read its ordered choices\n",
        "    Convert the choices from text to a list if needed\n",
        "    Read its zero-based answer position k\n",
        "    Set reference label y[i] to choices[k]\n",
        "    Display the row and highlight position k\n",
        "END FOR\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The rule is $y_i=\\mathrm{choices}_i[\\mathrm{correct\\_answer}_i]$. Here $i$ identifies the record and `correct_answer` gives the position $k_i$ **within that record**. Position 0 is the first choice and position 2 is the third."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "setup",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "setup"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Read and run. The data loader makes public Hugging Face requests.\n",
        "\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import time\n",
        "from io import BytesIO\n",
        "from urllib.error import HTTPError, URLError\n",
        "from urllib.parse import urlencode\n",
        "from urllib.request import urlopen\n",
        "\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from IPython.display import Image as NotebookImage, display\n",
        "\n",
        "import ast\n",
        "\n",
        "DATA_SERVER = \"https://datasets-server.huggingface.co\"\n",
        "ROBOT = \"keplerccc/Robo2VLM-1\"\n",
        "TARGET_IDS = (\"14652_q29\", \"14652_q35\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def read_url(url):\n",
        "    for attempt in range(3):\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            with urlopen(url, timeout=25) as response:\n",
        "                return response.read()\n",
        "        except (URLError, TimeoutError) as error:\n",
        "            if isinstance(error, HTTPError) and error.code not in {429, 500, 502, 503, 504}:\n",
        "                raise RuntimeError(f\"Hugging Face returned HTTP {error.code}. Rerun the data cell.\") from error\n",
        "            if attempt == 2:\n",
        "                raise RuntimeError(\"Hugging Face is unavailable. The saved default outputs can support discussion.\") from error\n",
        "            time.sleep(2 ** attempt)\n",
        "\n",
        "def page(dataset, offset=0, first=False):\n",
        "    params = {\"dataset\": dataset, \"config\": \"default\", \"split\": \"train\"}\n",
        "    endpoint = \"first-rows\" if first else \"rows\"\n",
        "    if not first:\n",
        "        params.update(offset=offset, length=100)\n",
        "    return json.loads(read_url(f\"{DATA_SERVER}/{endpoint}?{urlencode(params)}\"))[\"rows\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "def show_figure(fig):\n",
        "    buffer = BytesIO()\n",
        "    fig.savefig(buffer, format=\"png\", dpi=125, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
        "    plt.close(fig)\n",
        "    display(NotebookImage(data=buffer.getvalue()))"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "load-robot-rows",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "load-robot-rows"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Read and run. Each row has its own choice order.\n",
        "def reference_answer(row):\n",
        "    choices = row[\"choices\"]\n",
        "    choices = ast.literal_eval(choices) if isinstance(choices, str) else choices\n",
        "    return choices[row[\"correct_answer\"]]\n",
        "\n",
        "first_robot = [entry[\"row\"] for entry in page(ROBOT, first=True)]\n",
        "targets = [next(row for row in first_robot if row[\"id\"].endswith(key)) for key in TARGET_IDS]"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "measurement-run",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "measurement-run"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2 · Decode and display the result\n",
        "\n",
        "**Your turn.** Predict the reference for each row before running the default. Then set FOCUS to **\"q29\"** or **\"q35\"** to inspect one row at a time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "measure-fit",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "measure-fit",
        "outputId": "6b71804b-770b-4d9a-c24d-a3c600a895cf"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Your turn. Keep the default first. Then try \"q29\" or \"q35\".\n",
        "FOCUS = \"both\"  # \"both\", \"q29\" or \"q35\"\n",
        "assert FOCUS in {\"both\", \"q29\", \"q35\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "visible = [row for row in targets if FOCUS == \"both\" or row[\"id\"].endswith(FOCUS)]\n",
        "records = []\n",
        "for row in visible:\n",
        "    options = ast.literal_eval(row[\"choices\"]) if isinstance(row[\"choices\"], str) else row[\"choices\"]\n",
        "    records.append({\n",
        "        \"Frame\": \"_\".join(row[\"id\"].split(\"_\")[-2:]),\n",
        "        \"Stored index\": row[\"correct_answer\"],\n",
        "        **{str(i): label for i, label in enumerate(options)},\n",
        "        \"Reference\": reference_answer(row),\n",
        "    })\n",
        "measured = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "display(measured)\n",
        "\n",
        "# The highlighted column marks the stored index in each row.\n",
        "cols = [\"Frame\", \"0\", \"1\", \"2\", \"3\", \"Reference\"]\n",
        "colors = [[\"#deefed\" if col == str(row[\"Stored index\"]) else \"#ffffff\"\n",
        "           for col in cols] for row in records]\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 1.75), layout=\"constrained\", facecolor=\"#f6fbfb\")\n",
        "ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "t = ax.table(cellText=measured[cols].values, colLabels=cols, cellColours=colors,\n",
        "             colColours=[\"#d9e5ea\"]*len(cols), cellLoc=\"center\",\n",
        "             colWidths=[.12,.16,.20,.17,.20,.11], bbox=[.02,.15,.96,.66])\n",
        "t.auto_set_font_size(False)\n",
        "t.set_fontsize(9)\n",
        "for cell in t.get_celld().values():\n",
        "    cell.set_edgecolor(\"#c9d8df\")\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Robo2VLM-1  |  Decode the index within each frame\", color=\"#102b3d\", fontsize=14)\n",
        "show_figure(fig)"
      ],
